You are given:
1. A chart image
2. Base visualization code
3. A user instruction

The user instruction is the highest priority. It defines what must be fixed, changed, transformed, or matched.

Your output will be evaluated by visual similarity to the reference image. Maximize visual fidelity wherever possible.

Intent:
Style-Aware Error Repair

Task:
The image is the target chart style/output and may show marked potential errors. The base code may generate a different or incomplete chart. Recreate the clean reference chart as closely as possible while avoiding the marked or anticipated issues.

Important rules:
- Return only the complete corrected code.
- Do not include explanation.
- Do not include markdown fences.
- If the input code is Python/Matplotlib, return complete Python code.
- If the input code is Vega-Lite, return complete valid Vega-Lite JSON.
- Preserve the original data meaning unless the instruction or reference chart requires transformation.
- Match the reference chart as closely as possible in chart type, data values, encodings, colors, fonts, title, labels, axes, legend, annotations, layout, spacing, aspect ratio, and overall appearance.
- For Correctness Repair and Quality Improvement, fix the issue while keeping the clean corrected chart visually similar to the shown chart.
- For all other intents, treat the image as the target chart and recreate it as closely as possible.
- Ignore handwritten marks unless they indicate issues to fix.
- Do not reproduce handwritten notes, circles, arrows, or error markings.

Language / Library:
vegalite


Question:
By how many percentage points does the proportion of those who 'are worn out' by the amount of news exceed those who 'like' the amount of news within the political group that shows the greatest such difference?

Table Data:
Entity, Like the amount of news, by Are worn out the amount of news
Dem /Lean Dem, 40, 59
Re p/Lean Rep, 24, 75
Total, 32, 66

User Instruction:
Reorganize the three charts into a horizontal row to reduce vertical length and scrolling. Position the orange 'Rep/Lean Rep' chart first, followed by the red and blue charts, and also put the title lower to decrease the length of the image for better readability.

Base Code:
{
  "$schema": "https://vega.github.io/schema/vega-lite/v5.json",
  "data": {
    "values": [
      {"Entity": "Dem /Lean Dem", "Like": 40, "Worn Out": 59},
      {"Entity": "Rep /Lean Rep", "Like": 24, "Worn Out": 75},
      {"Entity": "Total", "Like": 32, "Worn Out": 66}
    ]
  },
  "transform": [
    {"calculate": "datum['Worn Out'] - datum['Like']", "as": "Difference"}
  ],
  "mark": "bar",
  "encoding": {
    "x": {
      "field": "Entity",
      "type": "nominal",
      "axis": {"title": "Political Group"}
    },
    "y": {
      "field": "Difference",
      "type": "quantitative",
      "axis": {"title": "Difference in Percentage Points"}
    },
    "color": {
      "field": "Entity",
      "type": "nominal",
      "legend": null,
      "scale": {"range": ["#1f77b4", "#ff7f0e", "#2ca02c"]}
    }
  },
  "title": "Difference in Percentage Points: 'Worn Out' vs 'Like' by Political Group",
  "config": {
    "axis": {
      "labelAngle": 0,
      "labelFontSize": 12,
      "titleFontSize": 14
    },
    "title": {
      "fontSize": 16,
      "anchor": "start"
    }
  }
}

Return only the complete corrected code.

code:
{
  "$schema": "https://vega.github.io/schema/vega-lite/v5.json",
  "data": {
    "values": [
      {"Entity": "Twitter.com", "Values": 50.0},
      {"Entity": "Organization or group", "Values": 53.0},
      {"Entity": "Celebrities", "Values": 62.0},
      {"Entity": "News and current events", "Values": 66.0},
      {"Entity": "Commercial product", "Values": 73.0},
      {"Entity": "Sports", "Values": 76.0},
      {"Entity": "Adult content", "Values": 90.0}
    ]
  },
  "transform": [
    {"aggregate": [{"op": "sum", "field": "Values", "as": "Total"}]},
    {"calculate": "datum.Total / 7", "as": "Expected"},
    {"calculate": "(datum.Values - datum.Expected) / datum.Expected * 100", "as": "Deviation"}
  ],
  "mark": "bar",
  "encoding": {
    "x": {
      "field": "Entity",
      "type": "nominal",
      "axis": {"labelAngle": -45},
      "title": "Category"
    },
    "y": {
      "field": "Deviation",
      "type": "quantitative",
      "title": "Deviation from Expected (%)"
    },
    "color": {
      "condition": {
        "test": "datum.Entity === 'Adult content'",
        "value": "red"
      },
      "value": "steelblue"
    }
  },
  "title": "Deviation from Expected Contribution by Category",
  "config": {
    "axis": {
      "labelFontSize": 12,
      "titleFontSize": 14
    },
    "title": {
      "fontSize": 16
    }
  }
}

{
  "$schema": "https://vega.github.io/schema/vega-lite/v5.json",
  "description": "Chart showing the share of population with the characteristic by age group.",
  "data": {
    "values": [
      {"age": "18-34", "share": 75},
      {"age": "35-44", "share": 68},
      {"age": "45-54", "share": 63},
      {"age": "55-64", "share": 47},
      {"age": "65+", "share": 32}
    ]
  },
  "mark": "line",
  "encoding": {
    "x": {
      "field": "age",
      "type": "ordinal",
      "title": "Age Group",
      "axis": {"labelAngle": 0}
    },
    "y": {
      "field": "share",
      "type": "quantitative",
      "title": "Share of Population (%)"
    }
  },
  "layer": [
    {
      "mark": "point",
      "encoding": {
        "color": {"value": "steelblue"}
      }
    },
    {
      "mark": "text",
      "encoding": {
        "text": {"field": "share", "type": "quantitative"},
        "x": {"field": "age", "type": "ordinal"},
        "y": {"field": "share", "type": "quantitative"},
        "color": {"value": "black"}
      },
      "transform": [
        {"calculate": "datum.share + '%'", "as": "share"}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "title": "Share of Population with Characteristic by Age Group",
  "config": {
    "axis": {
      "labelFontSize": 12,
      "titleFontSize": 14
    },
    "title": {
      "fontSize": 16,
      "anchor": "start"
    }
  }
}

