Question:
What is the magnitude (in percentage points) of the largest decrease in the share of the population with the characteristic between any two consecutive age groups?

Table Data:
Characteristic, Share of population
18-34, 75%
35-44, 68%
45-54, 63%
55-64, 47%
65+, 32%
Total, 59%

User Instruction:
Widen the chart canvas horizontally to resolve X-axis label overlap and provide spacing between categories. Add solid circular markers at every recorded measurement point along the line to clearly define each age group's data.

